{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-007","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as \"Polyurethene\" (a polymer) while also specifying \"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)\" (Iron Zinc Blue Passivated, a metallic plating process). Polyurethane cannot receive zinc electroplating, creating a direct conflict that makes the part impossible to manufacture as specified. The designer must correct either the material or the surface treatment so they are compatible."

  ,
  "recommended_correction": "Change the surface treatment to one applicable to polyurethane, or change the material to a metal if zinc plating is required."}]}
